  "conclusions": [
    "There is a strong relationship between Public Space users' activities and their Psychological stress through sensory experience.",
    "Key external stressors increasing psychological stress include noise (from traffic and street vendors), permanent attention demands (from pedestrian/vehicle movement, safety, overcrowding), and lack of space cleanness/pollution.",
    "Key factors reducing psychological stress include organized public space elements (street furniture, lighting, shading, movement), green areas, water features (due to calming colors and noise reduction), separation of traffic, and social activities that foster enjoyment and happiness.",
    "Architects, urban space designers, and planners have a crucial role in creating non-stressed psychological public spaces."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The study is a case study focused on a specific urban public space in Tripoli, Lebanon, which may limit generalizability.",
    "The sample size for the questionnaire survey was relatively small (N=65)."
  ],
